<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at key Brazilian ports.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping soybeans and soy products:</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: El Flamenco loading 18,900 tonnes soymeal. Blessing loading 56,500 tonnes soymeal. Theonymphus loading 31,186 tonnes soybeans/meal. Waiting to dock, 10 vessels to load soymeal, three to load soybeans and one for mixed cargo (soybeans/meal). Road: no figures available.</p>
<p>Loading (July 25-27): 62,237 tonnes soybeans, 50,629 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: At public terminal, Cornilios loading 51,000 tonnes soymeal. Waiting to dock, one vessel to load 12,000 tonnes soybeans and one to load 30,000 tonnes soybeans. At Cutrale terminal, Commander loading 67,007 tonnes soymeal. No vessels docked at Cargill private terminal. Waiting to dock, one vessel to load 60,000 tonnes soymeal and one to load 30,250 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Road: 32 trucks carrying 814 tonnes soybeans arrived on July</p>
<p>27.</p>
<p>Rail: none.</p>
<p>Loading (July 27): none.</p>
<p>Stocks: 35,899 tonnes soybeans, 5,874 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
